From cf92e2789f32886881126a36abb9adb4b42391ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jelle Feringa <jelleferinga@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 15:01:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Split range bounds in the joint velocity, acceleration
 and jerk constraints

The bounds constructors take the RangeBoundHandling argument that
JointPosConstraint and CartPosConstraint have, defaulting to
kSplitToTwoInequalities. Each range row becomes a lower-bound row followed by
an upper-bound row; equality and one-sided rows stay single rows, so the
bounds may mix all three per joint. A symmetric band -v <= dq <= v can then be
a TrajOptQPProblem constraint, which rejects unsplit range rows.

Each class keeps a row map from output row to difference row (timestep *
n_dof + joint), and getValues(), getJacobian() and the coefficients follow it.
splitRangeBounds() and selectRows() in ifopt_utils do the work for all three.
Targets are equality bounds and never split.

Refs #606
